{"id":"G0622","lemma":"ἀπολλύω","transliteration":"apolluō","sayIt":"apolluō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to destroy","meaning":"ἀπ-όλλυμι and ἀπολλύω\n[in LXX for אָבַד, etc. (38 words in all)].\n1. Act.,\n1 to destroy utterly, destroy, kill: Mk 124, 922, al.; τ. ψνχήν, Mat.10:28, al.;\n2 to lose utterly: Mat.10:42, al.; metaphorically, of failing to save, Jhn.6:39 18:9.\n2. Mid.,\n1 to perish;\n(a) of things: Mat.5:29, Jhn.6:12, Heb.1:11 (LXX, al.;\n(b) of persons: Mat.8:26, al. Metaphorical, of loss of eternal life, Jhn.3:15-16 10:28 17:12, Rom.2:12, 1Co.8:11 15:18, 2Pe.3:9. In οἱ ἀπολλὺμενοι, the perishing, contrasted in 1Co.1:18, al., with οἱ σωζόμενοι, the \"perfective\" force of the verb, WH. \" implies the completion of the process of destruction,\" is illustrated (see M, Pr., 114 f.; M, Th., ii, 2:10);\n2 to be lost: Luk.15:4 21:18. Metaphorical, on the basis of the relation between shepherd and flock, of spiritual destitution and alienation from God: Mat.10:6 15:24, Luk.19:10 (MM, see word; DCG, i, 191 f., ii, 76, 554; Cremer, 451)\n(AS)","glosses":["lose","lost","perishing","destroy","kill","perish"],"count":84,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-2","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"to kill","kjv":"to destroy"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":29,"renderings":{"bsb":"lose","kjv":"should perish"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":30,"renderings":{"bsb":"lose","kjv":"should perish"}},{"chapterId":"mat-8","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"We are perishing"}},{"chapterId":"mat-9","v":17,"renderings":{"bsb":"will be ruined","kjv":"perish"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"lost","kjv":"the lost"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":28,"renderings":{"bsb":"destroy","kjv":"to destroy"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":39,"renderings":{"bsb":"will lose","kjv":"shall lose"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":42,"renderings":{"bsb":"he will never lose","kjv":"lose"}},{"chapterId":"mat-12","v":14,"renderings":{"bsb":"they might kill","kjv":"they might destroy"}},{"chapterId":"mat-