eph in a dream, saying, “Arise and take the young child and his mother, and flee into…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Mark 1:24","note":"saying, “Ha! What do we have to do with you, Jesus, you Nazarene? Have you come to destroy us? I know you who you are: the Holy One of God!”","source":"web"},{"ref":"Luke 4:34","note":"saying, “Ah! what have we to do with you, Jesus of Nazareth? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are: the Holy One of God!”","source":"web"},{"ref":"John 3:16","note":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his one and only Son, that whoever believes in him should not perish, but have eternal life.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Acts 5:37","note":"After this man, Judas of Galilee rose up in the days of the enrollment, and drew away some people after him. He also perished, and all, as many as obeyed him…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Romans 2:12","note":"For as many as have sinned without the law will also perish without the law. As many as have sinned under the law will be judged by the law.","source":"web"},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 1:18","note":"For the word of the cross is foolishness to those who are dying, but to us who are being saved it is the power of God.","source":"web"},{"ref":"2 Corinthians 2:15","note":"For we are a sweet aroma of Christ to God, in those who are saved and in those who perish:","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}